# Every image and tool the scans run. CI reads them from here and nowhere else.
#
# The three GitLab analyzers are MIT-licensed, so they may run outside GitLab.
# Dependency Scanning (gemnasium) and DAST are under the GitLab Enterprise
# Edition licence and are not run here; Container Scanning with language
# packages turned on covers the dependencies instead.
#
# THE ANALYZERS ARE NAMED BY TAG, ON PURPOSE. GitLab publishes each analyzer
# again under the same tags and deletes the build a tag named before. The
# digests pinned here on 2026-10-28 were gone by 11-01, and the ones pinned on
# 11-01 were gone by 11-03 ("manifest unknown"). Exact versions move too:
# secrets 7.41.0 ran here from one digest on 10-28 and its tag names another
# today. A digest from that registry holds for days, and a pin that breaks
# every week is a scan that does not run.
#
# So they are named by major tag, the way GitLab's own CI templates name their
# analyzers, and the scan runs what a GitLab pipeline would pull that day.
# scripts/scan-gitlab.sh pulls each one once, runs the digest it pulled, and
# writes that digest and the analyzer's version into reports/analyzers.json.
SEMGREP_IMAGE=registry.gitlab.com/security-products/semgrep:7
SECRETS_IMAGE=registry.gitlab.com/security-products/secrets:7
CONTAINER_SCANNING_IMAGE=registry.gitlab.com/security-products/container-scanning:8
# These two publishers keep what they publish: pinned by digest and by checksum.
REGISTRY_IMAGE=registry:2@sha256:a3d8aaa63ed8681a604f1dea0aa03f100d5895b6a58ace528858a7b332415373
SNYK_CLI_VERSION=1.1308.3
SNYK_CLI_SHA256=5f323f45885341ea1473639859271925912ece82a2f77bc146bb4468f9838840
